(footprint "LitzPad_15A"
  (version 20240108)
  (generator "hand-built")
  (descr "High-current litz wire termination pad, 15A rated. 8.0 mm dia pad, 3.0 mm dia hole. Dimension sourcing: generic high-current PTH pad spec; low confidence — no part-specific datasheet exists for this custom coil terminal. Flagged for human visual cross-check before fabrication. PITCH CORRECTED 2026-07-29 (docs/brainstorms/2026-07-29-hv-footprint-copper-shorts-requirements.md Case 2): this is R30, Sheetpath tank.inductor_conn -- the two ends of the resonant tank coil itself (pad 1 net tank.c_tank1-p2, pad 2 net tank-out; elec/src/modules.ato). The prior 5.0mm pitch on 8.0mm pads gave -3.0mm (3.0mm of copper OVERLAP), a fabrication-blocking short between the tank's two highest-differential-voltage nodes, unconditionally wrong regardless of the voltage question below. That 2026-07-29 revision set the pitch to 13.0mm = 8.0mm pad dia + 5.0mm creepage (SUPERSEDED 2026-08-12, see below; retained here because the reasoning that replaced it is only legible against it), where 5.0mm is docs/specs/HIGH_VOLTAGE_CLEARANCE_SPEC.md Sec 5.1's IEC 60335-1 Table 16 (Pollution Degree 2, Material Group IIIb) BASIC-insulation creepage figure at 400V -- the applicable category since both pads are the same tank circuit (not a mains/SELV boundary; c.f. scripts/generate_kicad_dru.py's separately-lower 'HV internal same footprint' 1.5mm, which is a TO-247-pin-pitch compromise for a manufacturer-fixed package and does not apply here since this footprint's geometry is fully our own choice). 400V is elec/src/modules.ato's declared v_tank_peak (asserted design floor, used elsewhere for c_tank1/c_tank2 voltage-rating margin). CAVEAT (1) OF THAT NOTE IS NOW CLOSED, AND IT RESOLVED AGAINST THE 13.0mm PITCH -- PITCH RE-DERIVED 2026-08-12 TO 18.0mm. The 2026-07-29 note said: 'if the finalized L pushes working voltage above 400V, this 13.0mm/5.0mm figure is a floor, not sufficient, and must be re-derived at the higher voltage ... a >400V case needs a fresh standard lookup, not extrapolation from this table'. That condition is met: the tank node's working voltage is now MEASURED, not assumed, at 570.5 Vrms / 923.7 V peak (docs/evidence/2026-08-12-hv-clearance-adequacy.md; this pad pair specifically carries tank.c_tank1-p2 <-> tank-out, i.e. essentially the tank<->PWR_RTN voltage at 544.6 Vrms -- same Table 18 row). The fresh lookup was done and it is a DIFFERENT table and a different pollution degree from the superseded one: IEC 60335-1 Table 18 (functional insulation creepage), band >500-800V, material group IIIa/IIIb, POLLUTION DEGREE 3 -> 10.0mm. PD3 governs, not the PD2 this footprint's previous derivation used: IEC 60335-2-6 cl. 29.2's Addition makes PD3 the default for cooking appliances, and the sealed compartment PD2 would be conditional on is both unbuilt and thermally counterproductive (docs/evidence/2026-08-12-pollution-degree-resolution.md; docs/evidence/2026-08-11-pd2-decision-record.md; docs/evidence/2026-08-12-hv-hv-creepage-determination.md for the Table 18 derivation). So the PD3/Table 18 lookup SUPERSEDES the PD2/Table 16 400V lookup that produced 13.0mm -- that older figure is not a floor that happened to be raised, it was read from a table that does not apply to this node. New pitch 18.0mm = 8.0mm pad dia + 10.0mm creepage; measured pad-edge-to-pad-edge gap is exactly 10.0mm. Coating this pair down to PD1 was considered and is NOT available: IEC 60664-3 cl. 4.3 requires the conductive part to be COVERED by the coating, and these two pads are bare litz-wire terminations that must stay uncoated to be soldered to. (2) STILL OPEN, unchanged and NOT closed by this revision, flagged for human sign-off before fabrication: the 8.0mm pad diameter itself remains the original 'generic ... low confidence, no part-specific datasheet' figure -- widening only the pitch does not source the diameter; confirm the actual lug/terminal size against a real 15A litz-wire termination spec before fabrication. Note that the diameter and the pitch are coupled: the 18.0mm pitch is derived AS 'diameter + 10.0mm', so if the diameter is later sourced at anything other than 8.0mm the pitch must move with it, or the 10.0mm creepage is silently lost.")
  (tags "litz custom coil terminal high_current")
  (attr through_hole)
  (pad "1" thru_hole circle (at 0 0) (size 8.0 8.0) (drill 3.0) (layers "*.Cu" "*.Mask"))
  (pad "2" thru_hole circle (at 18.0 0) (size 8.0 8.0) (drill 3.0) (layers "*.Cu" "*.Mask"))
)
